# Camera System

## Overview

AiTrainer uses Android's Camera API and CameraX library to capture real-time video feed for pose detection. The camera system handles initialization, frame processing, and provides the data needed for ML Kit's pose detection.

## Key Components

### Camera Activity
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CameraXLivePreviewActivity.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CameraXLivePreviewActivity.kt): Main camera preview activity that handles camera initialization, permissions, and ML Kit processing

### Camera Source
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CameraSource.java](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CameraSource.java): Manages camera configuration, frame capture, and preprocessing

### Camera Preview
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CameraSourcePreview.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/CameraSourcePreview.kt): UI component for displaying camera preview

### Graphics Overlay
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/GraphicOverlay.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/GraphicOverlay.kt): Canvas for drawing pose detection results over the camera feed

## Camera Workflow
1. The app requests camera permissions
2. CameraXLivePreviewActivity initializes the camera
3. Camera frames are continuously captured
4. Each frame is sent to the pose detector for processing
5. Results are visualized on the GraphicOverlay
6. User feedback is provided based on pose analysis
